# Story: someone with five windows, three of them out of view and one behind the window they look at, finds each by typing a
# few letters, whatever keeps it from being seen, and hops back to where they were with Return alone.
# Reference: A27 (docs/features/F27-window-finder.md). Window ids start at 101.
# Written by the executor swarm, 2026-10-14; for the documenter to review.
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
open Terminal
open Music
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
dock 105 beside 101 bottom
# Terminal (104) floats in the middle. Framed on Safari, what is docked is out of view; Terminal stays where it is, behind Safari.
focus 101
zoom 101
expect fills 101
expect hidden 102
expect hidden 103
expect hidden 105
expect still 104
expect visible 104
expect at 104 300 200 640x420
expect in-front 101
# ⌃⌥G, "no", Return: the level is kept, so Notes is framed as Safari was.
find
expect ok
finder-type no
finder-choose
expect ok
expect fills 103
expect hidden 101
# Return straight after ⌃⌥G goes back to the window before this one, and frames that.
find
finder-choose
expect fills 101
expect hidden 103
# Escape changes nothing.
zoom 101
find
finder-type mail
finder-cancel
expect fills 101
expect hidden 102
# Without the palette, for scripts and shortcuts.
find music
expect ok
expect fills 105
expect hidden 101
# From a group the view steps out just far enough to show both.
zoom 102
out
expect visible 103
expect hidden 105
find music
expect ok
expect visible 105
expect visible 102
# A floating window is in view already: it comes to the front and gets the keyboard, and no view moves.
zoom 101
find term
expect ok
expect still
expect visible 104
expect floating 104
expect focused 104
expect in-front 104
expect at 104 300 200 640x420
expect camera 101
expect fills 101
# A minimised window comes back from the Dock to its own place.
minimize 102
zoom 101
find mail
expect ok
expect fills 102
show-all
expect above 102 103
# Saved views are in the same list.
zoom 103
save-view 3
show-all
find
finder-type v3
finder-choose
expect fills 103
# Nothing matches: it says so and nothing moves.
find zebra
expect fail
expect fills 103
# The window chosen has closed meanwhile: the palette stays open with a fresh list.
find
finder-type music
close 105
finder-choose
expect ok
expect fills 103
finder-type safari
finder-choose
expect visible 101
expect count docked 3
